    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/01/mizuno-wave-rebellion-pro-3-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ultra-high 61/57 mm stack and improved midsole compliance suggest strong impact protection, with the best heel/forefoot feel for midfoot or forward-heel strikers.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is described as more resilient than v2, and the aggressive geometry is built for faster efforts, delivering a race-oriented rebound rather than a relaxed easy-pace ride.",
        "Stability: Stability is mixed; the very tall, aggressive platform may feel unstable for some and the heel counter is very flexible (with some heel slippage noted), but midfoot lockdown and lateral/frontal-plane control are generally good when laced securely.",
        "Durability: Outsole wear and long-term material longevity are not clearly reported in the provided text; the light mesh upper is breathable but showed mild abrasion potential when run sockless."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/01/mizuno-wave-rebellion-pro-3-review-8.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The midsole feels very soft and almost bottomless at heel impact, with cushioning most pronounced just in front of the heel and a less evenly distributed forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is a standout (described as explosive and 10/10), with huge bounce and a snappy late transition, though the very tall stack causes a longer compression/release phase.",
        "Stability: Stability is a clear weakness—split/beveled heel geometry and high stack make landings less stable than competitors, and the reviewer reports ankle strain risk despite a very rigid plate and secure upper lockdown.",
        "Durability: Outsole traction and full coverage are praised, but the prominent toe-area nubs are expected to wear relatively quickly; upper materials are described as strong and long-lasting."
      ]
    }
